\section{File format}{

All integers are little-endian and offsets are counted from 0.

\strong{Header.} Bytes \verb{02 33 32 00}, then the length-prefixed string
\verb{REGISTER FILE} at 0x04 and a length-prefixed container version at 0x18:
\code{notused} in files from revisions B and C, \code{A.xx.xx} in files from
revision A. At 0x22 is a u32 offset of the object index and at 0x26 a u16
object count. The index holds one 8-byte entry per object, starting with the
u32 offset of the object; the index itself begins where the last object
ends.

\strong{Revision B and C objects.} A 12-byte preamble, whose contents differ by
revision, then a stream written by the 'MFC' \code{CArchive} class. Each object
starts with a u16 tag: \code{FFFF} introduces a new class (u16 schema, u16 name
length, ASCII name); \code{8000} plus an index refers to a class already read;
\verb{7FFF} is followed by a u32 tag for large indices. Class indices restart in
every object. The classes are:
\itemize{
\item \code{CHPUserObject} and \code{CHPLCObject}: two objects (the second a list of
keys and values), then a flag byte and, if it is set, a data object.
\item \code{CHPList}: one object. \code{CObArray}: a u16 count (\code{FFFF} then a u32 count
when large) followed by that many objects.
\item \code{CHPNdrDouble}, \code{CHPNdrString} and \code{CHPNdrObject}: a key, 6 bytes, then a
float64, a string or a flag byte and object. Strings are a u16 length
followed by UTF-16LE; a length of \code{C000} is instead followed by a u16 id
naming a standard key (0 \code{ObjClass}, 1 \code{Title}).
\item \code{CHPDatLongSliced} and \code{CHPDatDoubleSliced}: 6 bytes, then the y row and
the x row.
\item \code{CHPDatLongRow} and \code{CHPDatDoubleRow}: 14 bytes, the unit string, u16 \code{7},
u16, u32 point count n and a u8 flag marking an implicit row. Unless
implicit, n int32 (\code{Long}) or float64 (\code{Double}) values follow. Then u32,
float64 first value, u8, u32 flag marking scaled values, float64 scale and
float64 offset. Values are raw x scale + offset if scaled and raw
otherwise; an implicit row is first + i x scale.
\item \code{CHPAnnText} and \code{CHPTable} are read past but not returned.
}

In \code{LCDIAG.REG} each trace is an object whose \code{Title} names it. Revision
B.01 stores traces as \code{CHPLCObject} with \code{CHPDatLong} rows and an implicit
time axis; B.04 does the same but writes a space before the comma in trace
names (\code{"PMP1 , Pressure"}), which is removed; revision C stores them as
\code{CHPUserObject} with unscaled \code{CHPDatDouble} rows and explicit, possibly
uneven, times. The other objects, titled \verb{Start/Stop Conditions}, hold only
keys and values.

\strong{Revision A objects.} One byte, a u32 record count n, n 16-byte record
headers (u16, u16 type, u32 size, u32, u32 id), 4n further bytes, then the
data of each record in turn. Records refer to one another by id. Types
\code{8001} and \code{8003} are Latin-1 strings and \code{8006} a string after 2 bytes;
\code{8002} holds a numeric array; \code{0602} (43 bytes) a key at byte 14 and float64
at byte 35; \code{0601} a key and the u32 id of its value at byte 35. Types
\code{0501} and \code{0503} (161 bytes) describe a trace: u32 point count at byte 9,
then the u32 ids of the x unit and data and the x scale at bytes 27, 31 and
61, and those of y at bytes 94, 98 and 128. An array id with no record
denotes an implicit axis of i x scale.

Not known: the meaning of the skipped bytes, and whether the scale or the
offset comes first in a row (every file seen has an offset of 0).
